claimed: theory-linearity — write the merge-scaling-shape result into the documentation where it belongs, above all into the theory textbook: docs/theory/04-free-freer.md's "left-nested-bind problem" section already names Voigtlander's codensity and van der Ploeg & Kiselyov's type-aligned sequences, and already declares that okay takes a third road (normalize in the one interpreter). The scaling sweep is that road's empirical vindication -- and the honest account of WHY the famous fix would buy nothing here (the shapes the library builds are right-nested). Plus docs/guide.md: the per-element price of the program-shaped merge against the chunked path, so a reader choosing between them has the number.
